notes               = "Untitled in source. Three plants named by colour rather than species — bitter green, dark moonlit, burnt gray-and-white — which is a painter's taxonomy, not a botanist's. The question is asked and never answered: she laughs, and knows. ۱۳۶۸/۱۱/۲۵ is 25 Bahman = 14 February 1990. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

گفتم سه گیاه را در کویر می‌شناسم...
گیاهِ دلتنگِ باران...
با رنگِ سبزِ تلخ...
گیاهِ هجرانی...
به رنگِ مهتابی تاریک...
و گیاهِ سوخته... خاکستری و سفید...
از تو می‌پرسم...
من از کدام گیاهم؟...
تو می‌خندی...
با نگاهی ابری و خاطری بارانی...
تو... می‌دانی...
۱۳۶۸/۱۱/۲۵

===machine===

I said I know three plants in the desert...
The plant that longs for rain...
in a bitter green...
The plant of separation...
in the color of dark moonlight...
and the burnt plant... gray and white...
I ask you...
which of these plants am I?...
You laugh...
with a clouded gaze and a rainy heart...
You... know...
1368/11/25

===lantern===

I said: I know three plants in the desert...
the plant homesick for rain,
in a bitter green...
the plant of separation,
the colour of dark moonlight...
and the burnt plant... gray and white...
I ask you...
which of the three am I?...
You laugh...
with a clouded gaze and a rainy heart...
You... know...

1368/11/25

